Z||000000||Julian||01-14-2001||09:39 AM||||Is it normal for more white smoke to come out of the driver's side exhaust? Feels like it's hotter sooner too.<P>Oh, it's an 88 Mera (Formula)<P><p>[This message has been edited by Julian (edited 01-14-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||01-14-2001||12:04 PM||||Upon start up any moisture that has condensed within the exhaust system will turn to steam and exit the exhaust system.  Why it comes out more on one side than another is a mystery to me, but it comes out the passenger side of my GT and has done so since new, even with a new exhaust system.<P>If the white smoke continues after a few minutes, it may mean a coolent leak into the engine.  Not a good sign.  ||||reg||3
